":"nobach","g":"Nobah","fb":[["kenath-2","Kenath","","Named once, in Judges, and nowhere else.","place",1],["nobah","Nobah","Man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness","He took the Amorite town of Kenath east of the Jordan and renamed it after himself, and the town turns up again as a landmark on Gideon's route.","person",1]],"v":[4760,4760,6730]},"H5080":{"l":"נָדַח","x":"nâdach","d":"to push off; used in a great variety of applications, literally and figuratively (to expel, mislead, strike, inflict, etc.)","p":"naw-dakh'","t":"nadach","g":"a banished [one]","fb":[],"v":[5023,5277,5282,5285,5411,5446,5471,5709,5712,5725,8369,8370,8403,10004,11462,11635,12305,12990,13982,14830,16352,16595,17828,17895,17919,17971,17972,18163,18760,19155,19350,19485,19486,19491,19532,19605,19610,19648,19652,19683,19767,19952,20001,20072,20131,20162,20182,20541,21316,21328,21994,22330,22625,22838]},"H5036":{"l":"נָבָל","x":"nâbâl","d":"stupid; wicked (especially impious)","p":"naw-bawl'","t":"nabal","g":"a fool","fb":[],"v":[5764,5779,8114,8330,12900,13564,14080,14519,14719,15065,15069,16879,16893,17272,18263,18264,19367,20710]},"H5044":{"l":"נִבְשָׁן","x":"Nibshân","d":"Nibshan, a place in Palestine","p":"nib-shawn'","t":"nibshan","g":"Nibshan","fb":[["nibshan","Nibshan","","Six towns stood in Judah's wilderness by the western shore of the Dead Sea, and Nibshan was one. It is often put near En-gedi, without a firm site.","place",1]],"v":[6264]},"H5096":{"l":"נַהֲלָל","x":"Nahălâl","d":"Nahalal or Nahalol, a place in Palestine","p":"nah-hal-awl'","t":"nahalal","g":"Nahalal","fb":[["nahalal","Nahalal","Nahalol","A town in Zebulun, later given with its pastures to the Merarite Levites. Zebulun never drove out the Canaanites there and put them to forced labour instead. It is sometimes linked with Tell en-Nahl near the Kishon River.","place",3]],"v":[6336,6416,6539]},"H5035":{"l":"נֶבֶל","x":"nebel","d":"a skin-bag for liquids (from collapsing when empty); hence, a vase (as similar in