th a generous gift, kept David from killing his whole household. When she told Nabal ten days later what he had nearly brought on them, he seems to have had a stroke, and he died. David married Abigail.","person",18]],"v":[7864,7865,7866,7870,7871,7875,7880,7886,7886,7887,7895,7897,7897,7898,7899,7900,7900,7900,7933,7983,8051,8084]},"H5064":{"l":"נָגַר","x":"nâgar","d":"to flow; figuratively, to stretch out; causatively, to pour out or down; figuratively, to deliver over","p":"naw-gar'","t":"nagar","g":"are] spilled","fb":[],"v":[8370,13353,14848,15078,15094,19404,20402,21348,22582,22584]},"H5051":{"l":"נֹגַהּ","x":"nôgahh","d":"brilliancy (literally or figuratively)","p":"no'-gah","t":"nogahh","g":"brightness","fb":[],"v":[8615,8657,14129,16507,17737,18671,18823,18839,18854,20467,20476,20490,20491,20636,22320,22357,22442,22771,22778]},"H5050":{"l":"נָגַהּ","x":"nâgahh","d":"to glitter; causatively, to illuminate","p":"naw-gah'","t":"nagahh","g":"he illuminates","fb":[],"v":[8631,13280,13416,14145,17830,17915]},"H5028":{"l":"נְבָט","x":"Nᵉbâṭ","d":"Nebat, the father of Jeroboam I","p":"neb-awt'","t":"nebat","g":"of Nebat","fb":[["nebat","Nebat","Man living at the time of United Monarchy","Jeroboam's father, and he is only ever named in \"Jeroboam son of Nebat,\" the phrase the books of Kings use again and again for the king blamed for making idol worship the habit of the north.","person",25]],"v":[9134,9153,9166,9250,9286,9309,9314,9473,9532,9579,9765,9822,9873,9882,9920,9934,9943,9949,9953,10004,10180,11393,11397,11410,11459]},"H5022":{"l":"נָבוֹת","x":"Nâbôwth","d":"Naboth, an Israelite","p":"naw-both'","t":"naboth","g":"Naboth","fb":[["naboth","Naboth","Man living at the time of Divided Monarchy","His vineyard sat next to King Ahab's palace, and he would not sell it, because Israel's law kept family land in the family. Jezebel had false witnesses accuse him of blasphemy, he was stoned, and Ahab took the vineyard. Elijah met Ahab there and announced the end of his